{"availability":"available","full":"NARBEHOUSE/Benny-s-Accessibility-Hub-2.0","name":"Benny-s-Accessibility-Hub-2.0","description":"Ben is nonspeaking and quadriplegic with vision challenges who only has access to left and right head switches (space and return) ","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":70,"forks":13,"created":"2026-02-02T16:24:41Z","updated":"2026-10-02T21:36:37Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://www.narbehouse.com","topics":["2-step","accessibility","app","discord","gaming","keyboard","streaming","switch"],"demo":null,"color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:16.039Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:16.039Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:16.039Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:19:16.039Z","stars":70,"forks":13}],"technologies":[],"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:05.333Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A bespoke software suite for one- and two-switch accessibility, built with Electron.","This project provides an accessible computing environment designed for users who operate a computer with limited input methods (such as a single switch or two-button switch control). The hub includes games, communication tools, an AI-powered conversation board, journaling, media streaming control, and more — all navigable via switch scanning."],"features":["The games themselves (Benny's Baseball, Football, Bowling, Mini Golf, and a dozen-plus others) don't live in this repo. They're actively developed and kept up to date on bennyshub.com (source), and this hub sources them…","Live — the hub fetches the current game list from bennyshub.com and, when you pick a game, loads it straight from there in the same sandboxed iframe every tool uses. Requires an internet connection; always reflects…","Local fallback — if the live site can't be reached (offline, or it's down), the hub falls back to a locally cached copy of that specific game, if one has been synced.","Not available — if neither works (no internet and never synced), the hub says so rather than showing a broken game.","Games are Ben's actual switch-accessible builds, so each one already knows how to exit back to this hub (not a website menu) regardless of whether it was loaded from bennyshub.com or a local file — that's built into the…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NARBEHOUSE/Benny-s-Accessibility-Hub-2.0/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f4e08e2d8b984487033a7e192666aeeb5a958f84734fc865d44ace68447236eb","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:15:05.363Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:05.327Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-02T21:36:37Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A bespoke software suite for one- and two-switch accessibility, built with Electron.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NARBEHOUSE/Benny-s-Accessibility-Hub-2.0/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"This project provides an accessible computing environment designed for users who operate a computer with limited input methods (such as a single switch or two-button switch control). The hub includes games, communication tools, an AI-powered conversation board, journaling, media streaming control, and more — all navigable via switch scanning.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NARBEHOUSE/Benny-s-Accessibility-Hub-2.0/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Requires your own streaming service API keys — see timd-api.example.json","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NARBEHOUSE/Benny-s-Accessibility-Hub-2.0/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"f4e08e2d8b984487033a7e192666aeeb5a958f84734fc865d44ace68447236eb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NARBEHOUSE/Benny-s-Accessibility-Hub-2.0/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:05.328Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NARBEHOUSE/Benny-s-Accessibility-Hub-2.0/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:05.329Z","hash":"f4e08e2d8b984487033a7e192666aeeb5a95